# LocalCert: certificate (C′) of the quartic local lemma (`local/LOCAL_LEMMA.md` §3′)

GENERATED by `lean/gen/export_local_cert.py` from `lean/gen/LocalCert.template.lean`; do not edit the data block.

Statement proved (`Cprime`): for every `z ∈ ℝ¹⁴` orthogonal to the five kernel vectors
(rotation fields r₁ r₂ r₃ and the soft fields ŝ₁ ŝ₂, all with entries in K = ℚ(α)) and every `σ ∈ ℝ²`,

  ½⟨z,Hz⟩ + ⟨Γ m, z⟩ + (13/40)|s|⁴ ≥ (1/16)|z|² + (29/500)|s|⁴,
  m = (σ₁², σ₁σ₂, σ₂²),  |s|⁴ = (25/4)(σ₁²+σ₂²)²,

where `H` (14×14) and `Γ` (14×3) are the exported exact data over K (α = √(10+2√5) = 4 sin 72°).

Method (all exact, no floating point in the proof):
* elements of K are `Kel` = 4 rationals in the power basis of α, with α⁴ = 20α² − 80;
* the 17×17 matrix `M = [[½H − εI + KKᵀ, ½Γ], [½Γᵀ, c·G_θ]]` is *computed* from the data by `Kel`
  arithmetic (the penalty KKᵀ vanishes on W = ker(Kᵀ));
* `M = Lᵀ diag(D) L + E` with dyadic `L, D` (float LDLᵀ of M − 10⁻⁴·I, rounded), and `E` (entries in K)
  is shown diagonally dominant using rational enclosures of each entry on a rational box for α;
* the whole check is one `Bool` closed by `decide +kernel`.
`qform_dd_nonneg` and `list_sum_range_map` are copied from the upstream Coulomb proof
(huwngtran/thomson-n7-lean, `ThomsonN7/Solution.lean`, block CERT1).
-/

